# Banter in Dawn's Gate and the Howlers Pass (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is dawns_gate): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ dawns_gate_01_delphine_silas
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:silas_vane and at:dawns_gate and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Soot on the cobbles and the same red rag nailed to every door, Silas. Heavy hand with the paint.
interject name:silas_vane: And red windows up the hill. Management's watching the table. Even the smoke tastes of copper.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: My Fool is pulling faces at the slag heap, and he hasn't even a nose to wrinkle.
interject name:silas_vane: It's the boarded-up mine that bothers me. When a town shuts its only living, the game's rigged.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_02_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and at:dg_briar and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Three paces back from that hearth, Rook. Gruber keeps his onions dry, I'll give him that.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Low beams, hard on a tall shield. Quiet sort of night when nobody in the taproom sings.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That pot on the hob was a goat once. The mice in my lapels are twitching for a crust.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Let them have my share. And remind me to sigh before the stairs. Looks odd, sitting by a fire not breathing.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Breathe when you please. Just don't let that knocker clack while I'm shaking the beetles out of my head.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_cellar_03_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:dg_briar and flag.cellar_asked and not flag.cellar_outcome and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby has his nose to the flagstones by the third rack, Cordelia. He doesn't point at beer.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Clever dog. That mortar behind the barrels is decades fresher than the rest, and air leaks through it.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Damp lime, bruised hops, and the scent of someone the bricks couldn't keep out.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My six eyes just clicked at that draught. Stand back, Lucan. I love a surprise.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: I only hope whatever's behind it has better manners than the last thing we cornered in the dark.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_upper_04_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dg_briar and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Four beds under the eaves, and I don't even sleep. Barnaby can have my bolster, Lucan.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Most gracious. Though one clap of thunder and he forgets he's a harbinger of dread.
interject name:silas_vane: Better a dog under a coat than a shadow lagging behind you. Mine keeps staring at that chest.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Don't let the red light rattle your cards, friend. A quiet hand on the blanket, perhaps?
interject name:silas_vane: You're on. Provided the hound doesn't yip every time I palm an ace.
endif
-> END

~ mon_pass_05_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and at:mon_pass and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: The Crimson Rose receives all, says the sign. Delightfully thorough. Look at the bats pouring from that belfry.
interject name:silas_vane: When a house puts out a welcome sign on a dead mountain, check the fine print, friend.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Mind the loose slate. Look how the red windows light the stone like an artery.
interject name:silas_vane: My censer's swinging wider than it should, and the dead trees are leaning in to watch the deal.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Then let's climb and see what keeps those lamps burning all night.
endif
-> END

~ dawns_gate_06_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dawns_gate and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Renathyr's dead, Lucan, and those red windows still stare down like cheap stage lights.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The air by the well is cleaner, though. More river, less old blood. Barnaby's tail is up.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: My Fool had three puns ready for the smelter and dropped every one. This quiet gives my stitching a chill.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: They've lived under that tower a long time, Delphine. Give them an evening to learn it has no teeth.
endif
-> END

~ mon_pass_07_rook_silas
if name:rook_coldwake and name:silas_vane and at:mon_pass and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Loose slate is worse coming down than going up, Silas. Mind your footing.
interject name:silas_vane: Chalk one more tally in my ribs for Renathyr. Walking off with all our bones is the best hand there is.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Look at the pilgrims' cairn. Every stone stacked neat by folk who marched up to that gate.
interject name:silas_vane: Leave the stones to the bats. Come on, I'll remind you to breathe at the river road.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Fair enough. And keep your shadow on the path where I can see it.
endif
-> END
